{"tool":"exec_command","command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot = Path('.')\n\ndef read(path):\n    text = (root / path).read_text()\n    text = text.replace('/home/scott/Documents/siril/tightpsf/', '')\n    return text.rstrip() + '\\n'\n\ndef migrated_section(path):\n    return f\"\\n## Migrated Source: `{path}`\\n\\nThe content below was migrated from `{path}` so the old scattered file can be deleted after verification without losing information. Workspace-relative paths are used where paths appeared in the source.\\n\\n```markdown\\n{read(path)}```\\n\"\n\nchangelog = \"\"\"# Refactor Review Changelog\n\nThis is the canonical consolidated changelog for the refactor review. Current\nstatus lives in `review_refactor/STATUS.md`; active follow-up work lives in\n`review_refactor/TODO.md`.\n\n## Unreleased\n\n### Documentation Consolidation\n\n- Created `review_refactor/` as the canonical home for refactor review notes.\n- Added `review_refactor/STATUS.md` as the latest current-state audit.\n- Added `review_refactor/TODO.md` as the active remaining-work list.\n- Added `review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md` as the consolidated changelog.\n- Kept historical planning and review files unchanged.\n- Migrated the full informational content of the historical changelog files into this file.\n\n### Baseline And Planning\n\n- Created an itemized scoring/refactor backlog from the original score-change notes.\n- Established the fixability-weighted scoring model as the target model.\n- Recorded the hard-gate product decision as warning-only rather than fatal rejection.\n- Preserved report schema visibility for deprecated diagnostic fields while separating them from base score inputs.\n\n### Data Models And Profiles\n\n- Added star diagnostics for HFR, HFD, median star flux/SNR, star rejection rate, FWHM P90/median ratio, trailing angle median/stdev, centroid drift, double-star flag, flux throughput, and compact per-star samples.\n- Added channel diagnostics for tile-noise spread, row/column banding, calibration state, hot-pixel count, and warm-pixel count.\n- Added optics metadata for capture grouping.\n- Replaced the old confidence component with `transparency_signal` in component scores while retaining compatibility where needed.\n- Added fixability-weighted component weights: clipping/saturation 24, sharpness/focus 19, star shape/tracking 16, field consistency 15, transparency signal 11, signal/noise 7, sky/background 5, artifacts 3.\n- Added session weights for background median, trailing-angle spread, centroid drift, and star rejection rate.\n- Added profile thresholds for black clipping, saturation, HFR, trailing angle spread, centroid drift, banding, tile noise, star rejection rate, transparency flux drop, and confidence caps.\n\n### Measurements And Diagnostics\n\n- Extended star measurement to compute covariance, HFR, flux, normalized position samples, elongation-tail metrics, rejection rate, and trailing-angle diagnostics.\n- Added matched-star sample data for session throughput and centroid drift.\n- Added double-star flagging from PSF-fit tail and elongation-tail evidence.\n- Added tile-noise spread using masked tile dispersion so bright stars, clipped pixels, and hot-pixel-like outliers do not dominate the measurement.\n- Added row/column banding detection.\n- Added hot/warm pixel counts.\n- Added calibration-state detection from image metadata.\n- Added optics metadata extraction from available FITS headers.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Replaced `star_sample_confidence_score` with `transparency_signal_score`.\n- Kept star sample confidence as a cap on star-dependent components, with a lighter cap for transparency.\n- Removed roundness, eccentricity, FWHM axis ratio, field uniformity, tilt, curvature, and cloud/fog from direct base component scoring.\n- Kept `background_mad_scaled` as the preferred noise input with `background_sigma` as fallback and diagnostic/session signal.\n- Split clipping behavior into black clipping and saturation, with white clipping retained as a diagnostic/session signal.\n- Kept cosmic rays as a low-weight artifact penalty.\n- Made satellite and airplane trails zero the artifact component and emit error reasons while normal scoring continues.\n- Added metric family caps for sharpness, shape, noise/transparency, background, and defect groups.\n- Added numeric `stack_weight` as integration usefulness on a `0.0..1.0` scale, distinct from the human-facing quality score.\n- Made stack weight account for clipping, saturation, trails, low star confidence, poor throughput, focus outliers, elongation outliers, centroid drift, and negative session adjustment.\n- Kept hard-gate checks warning-only with concise severe data-loss warning reasons and `score_impact = 0.0`.\n\n### Session Behavior\n\n- Added session-relative metrics for FWHM, FWHM tail/spread, elongation tail, stars per megapixel, used-star count, background sigma, clipping, trailing-angle spread, centroid drift, background median, and star rejection rate.\n- Added matched-star session throughput inside compatible groups, with median-star-flux fallback when matched samples are insufficient.\n- Added centroid drift population from matched star offsets.\n- Added session adjustment penalties and bonuses with caps.\n- Added temporal diagnostics for focus drift, seeing drift, and cloud arrival.\n- Added capture grouping by filter, exposure, gain, offset, binning, camera, and optics, with `unknown` fallback.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- Added or preserved JSON, CSV, text, and HTML visibility for the new score components and diagnostics.\n- Added numeric `stack_weight` to frame and session outputs.\n- Added exported score weights.\n- Preserved deprecated diagnostic fields in reports where downstream users may rely on them.\n- Kept report schema versioned as `2.0` with score model `fixability_weighted_v1`.\n\n### Tests And Verification\n\n- Added or updated tests for component weights, confidence caps, transparency scoring, clipping split behavior, hard-gate warning behavior, stack-weight separation, metric family caps, session scoring, schema/report fields, HFR basics, and analysis diagnostics.\n- Current canonical status notes that focused coverage is still light for matched-star throughput, centroid drift, optics grouping, double-star flagging, masked tile-noise behavior, and soft-star HFR edge cases.\n- A fresh focused test run still needs to be completed and recorded.\n\"\"\"\nfor p in [\"score_changes/changelog.md\", \"next_change/changelog.md\"]:\n    changelog += migrated_section(p)\nPath('review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md').write_text(changelog)\n\ntodo = \"\"\"# Refactor Review TODO\n\nThis is the canonical active work list and migrated planning record for the refactor review. Completed historical work is summarized in `review_refactor/STATUS.md` and `review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md`. Historical TODO/source-plan content is preserved below so the old scattered files can be deleted after verification without losing information.\n\n## Active Work\n\n- [ ] Retune acceptance and review thresholds after the current metric mix.\n  - Establish expected score bands for representative clean, review, and reject frames.\n  - Update defaults or profile-specific thresholds only after documenting the rationale.\n  - Add tests that pin the chosen thresholds.\n\n- [ ] Add guiding/root-cause classification beyond generic trailing angle.\n  - Use existing trailing-angle median/stdev as input.\n  - Preserve the original formula/criterion from the scoring plan: `theta = 0.5 * arctan(2b/(a-c))`; low stdev below about 5 degrees indicates a systematic issue.\n  - Classify RA-like, Dec-like, mixed, or unknown guiding patterns only when evidence is strong enough.\n  - Keep the current generic trailing diagnostics visible even when no root cause is assigned.\n\n- [ ] Add backfocus/tilt optical-root-cause diagnostics.\n  - Correlate edge-star elongation/trailing direction with position from image center.\n  - Preserve the original root-cause categories: radiating = backfocus error, tangential = opposite error, uniform direction = tilt.\n  - Report backfocus-like, tilt-like, uniform-trailing-like, or unknown classifications.\n  - Keep `edge_center_ratio` and `psf_spatial_variation` as the existing scoring inputs unless the scoring policy is deliberately changed.\n\n- [ ] Add dew/frost diagnostics.\n  - Detect likely scattering from session-relative FWHM/HFR ratio shifts and transparency loss.\n  - Preserve the original heuristic: FWHM/HFR ratio shift relative to session average indicates light scattering.\n  - Report the diagnostic separately from base transparency scoring until validated.\n  - Add tests for stable seeing, haze/cloud, and dew/frost-like cases.\n\n- [ ] Decide whether to implement the exact original relative transparency-index heuristic or keep matched-star throughput as the replacement.\n  - Original heuristic: track median flux of the 20 brightest stars; a drop above 30% with stable noise indicates thin clouds; map to `transparency_signal_score`.\n  - Current implementation uses matched-star throughput where possible, with median-star-flux fallback.\n  - Document which behavior is canonical before closing this item.\n\n- [ ] Finish pixel-scale normalization policy.\n  - Preserve the original formula: `Pixel_Scale = (Pixel_Size_um / Focal_Length_mm) * 206.265`.\n  - Normalize FWHM tiers to arcseconds when pixel scale is available, or document why the current pixel-primary threshold model remains canonical.\n\n- [ ] Decide whether tile-noise grading should exactly match the original plan.\n  - Original plan: 8x8 grid, mask stars/trails/hot pixels, compute MAD per tile multiplied by 1.4826, and use the 25th percentile as the main metric.\n  - Current implementation has masked tile dispersion as a diagnostic measurement.\n\n- [ ] Improve focused test coverage for refactor completion behavior.\n  - Matched-star throughput and median-flux fallback.\n  - Throughput/cloud heuristic double-counting.\n  - Centroid drift population, z-score penalties, and stack-weight impact.\n  - `capture` grouping with full, partial, and missing metadata, including optics.\n  - Double-star flagging from PSF-fit tail plus elongation-tail evidence.\n  - Masked tile-noise behavior with stars, clipped pixels, and hot-pixel-like outliers.\n  - HFR behavior for misleading FWHM and soft-star cases.\n  - Support/confidence family behavior, or explicit documentation that confidence caps replace that group.\n\n- [ ] Run and record a fresh focused test set.\n  - Run scoring tests.\n  - Run session tests.\n  - Run report/output tests.\n  - Record the command, environment, and result in `review_refactor/STATUS.md` or `review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n- [ ] Optional cleanup: remove or archive duplicate/stale Phase 8 wording from historical changelog files.\n  - Do not change historical files unless explicitly requested.\n  - Keep `review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md` as the canonical consolidated changelog regardless.\n\n## Not Active Work\n\n- Warning-only hard gates are the current product decision.\n- Numeric `stack_weight` is implemented.\n- Matched-star throughput and centroid drift are implemented.\n- Optics-aware capture grouping is implemented.\n- Roundness and white clipping are no longer base score drivers.\n\"\"\"\nfor p in [\"score_changes/score_changes.md\", \"score_changes/TODO.md\", \"next_change/TODO.md\"]:\n    todo += migrated_section(p)\nPath('review_refactor/TODO.md').write_text(todo)\n\nstatus = \"\"\"# Refactor Review Status\n\nThis is the canonical current-state audit for the refactor review. Use\n`review_refactor/TODO.md` for active follow-up work and\n`review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md` for consolidated history.\n\n## Historical Source Files\n\nThese files were used as historical inputs and their informational content has\nbeen migrated into the canonical files under `review_refactor/`:\n\n- `review_refactor.md`\n- `change_review.md`\n- `new_review.md`\n- `next_change/changelog.md`\n- `next_change/TODO.md`\n- `score_changes/changelog.md`\n- `score_changes/score_changes.md`\n- `score_changes/TODO.md`\n\nThe latest status audit supersedes older contradictory findings, especially\nstale incomplete findings from prior reviews.\n\n## Correct/Complete\n\n- Scoring, session, reporting, model, schema, and changelog paths are mapped and reviewable.\n- Deprecated base-score inputs were cleaned up: roundness, eccentricity, FWHM axis ratio, tilt, curvature, field uniformity, and HFD remain diagnostic/reporting fields rather than base component score drivers.\n- Star-shape scoring uses elongation and elongation-tail metrics.\n- Clipping score uses black clipping and saturation separately; white clipping remains visible and participates in session diagnostics but is not a base clipping-score input.\n- Noise scoring prefers `background_mad_scaled` and falls back to `background_sigma`; sigma remains available for warnings and session diagnostics.\n- Field consistency uses `edge_center_ratio` and `psf_spatial_variation`.\n- Sky/background uses `background_gradient` and `vignetting_estimate`.\n- `cloud_fog_estimate` is not a direct base-score input; it remains available for warning details and temporal diagnostics.\n- `star_sample_confidence_0_100` is a reliability cap, not a standalone score component.\n- `transparency_signal_score` replaced the old confidence component in the score model.\n- Component weights match the fixability-weighted table and sum to 100.\n- Metric family caps exist and reduce related double-counting.\n- Hard gates are intentionally warning-only and emit `reason_details` with `score_impact = 0.0`.\n- `stack_weight` is numeric on a `0.0..1.0` scale and can diverge from `overall_score`.\n- JSON, CSV, HTML, and text outputs expose the score model, components, score weights, diagnostics, and numeric stack weight.\n- Session transparency uses matched-star throughput when star samples can be matched, with median-star-flux fallback.\n- Matched-star centroid drift is populated and participates in session z-scores, session adjustment, and stack weight.\n- The `capture` grouping preset includes filter, exposure, gain, offset, binning, camera, and optics with `unknown` fallback.\n- Double-star diagnostics use PSF-fit tail plus elongation-tail evidence.\n- Tile-noise spread masks bright stars, clipped pixels, and hot-pixel-like outliers before tile dispersion.\n- Consolidated changelog history now lives in `review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md`.\n- The full historical review/refactor audit content is migrated into this file below.\n\n## Partially Correct/Complete\n\n- Transparency scoring uses throughput, SNR, star density, rejection, and confidence-related fallback signals, but not every originally proposed transparency input is a direct base-score term.\n- `background_median` is a session-relative signal, not a base component score input.\n- Tile noise, banding, hot/warm pixels, and calibration state are diagnostics/reporting metrics rather than base score inputs.\n- HFR can override or support FWHM in sharpness scoring; HFD is diagnostic only.\n- Arcsecond FWHM adds a softness deduction when pixel scale is known, but primary thresholds remain pixel-based.\n- Session and family caps reduce overlap, but they do not mathematically prove no issue is ever counted twice.\n- Confidence is handled by caps rather than a separate support/confidence metric family.\n- Cloud/fog is secondary through warnings and temporal diagnostics, not a direct transparency-score helper.\n- Test coverage exists for key scoring and reporting behavior, but focused coverage is light for matched-star throughput, centroid drift, optics grouping, double-star flagging, masked tile-noise behavior, and soft-star HFR edge cases.\n- Current grouping behavior works, but tests do not exhaust every `capture` metadata permutation.\n- Historical changelogs recorded the work, but they had duplicate Phase 8 wording before consolidation.\n\n## Incorrect/Incomplete\n\n- Acceptance and review thresholds have not been retuned after the new metric mix.\n- Full RA/Dec guiding root-cause classification is not implemented.\n- Backfocus/tilt root-cause classification from trailing-angle/vector-position correlation is not implemented.\n- Dew/frost diagnostics from FWHM/HFR ratio shifts are not implemented.\n- A fresh focused test run has not been completed and recorded in the canonical review docs.\n\"\"\"\nfor p in [\"review_refactor.md\", \"change_review.md\", \"new_review.md\"]:\n    status += migrated_section(p)\nPath('review_refactor/STATUS.md').write_text(status)\nPY","files":["change_review.md","new_review.md","next_change/TODO.md","next_change/changelog.md","review_refactor.md","review_refactor/CHANGELOG.md","review_refactor/STATUS.md","review_refactor/TODO.md","score_changes/TODO.md","score_changes/changelog.md","score_changes/score_changes.md"],"category":"read_range"}
