{"tool":"exec_command","command":"tee scripts/batch_ops/audit/plans/20260625191819_plan.md >/dev/null <<'EOF'\n# Batch Ops Audit Fix Plan - 20260625191819\n\n## Source Audit\n\n- Results file: /home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/audit/results/20260625191819.md\n- Standards file: /home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/.script_standards.md\n- Menu file: /home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py\n\n## Summary\n\n- Standards issues to address: 4\n- Dynamic menu parser issues to address: 1\n- Optional non-standard issues to address: 0\n- Files expected to change: `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py`, `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py`, `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py`, `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/audit/changelogs/20260625191819_change.md`\n\n## Issue Map\n\n### `.script_standards.md` Issues\n\n- `batch_auto_bge.py`: AutoBGE tuning options are single-dash multi-character options only: `-npoints`, `-polydegree`, and `-rbfsmooth`.\n- `batch_auto_bge.py`: Missing `--verbose|-v` support.\n- `batch_graxpert.py`: Several argparse aliases are not documented in the `Script defaults` table.\n- `batch_graxpert.py`: Missing `--verbose|-v` support.\n\n### Dynamic Menu Parser Issues\n\n- `.batch_ops_menu.py`: `parse_script_defaults_docstring()` overwrites repeated `(behavior)` rows, so only the last behavior row remains available after parsing.\n\n### Optional Non-Standard Issues\n\n- No issues found.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### Task 1: Add standards-compliant AutoBGE option aliases and verbose support\n\n- Files: `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py`\n- Issues addressed: `batch_auto_bge.py` single-dash AutoBGE tuning options; `batch_auto_bge.py` missing `--verbose|-v`.\n- Planned change: Add long argparse aliases `--npoints`, `--polydegree`, and `--rbfsmooth` while preserving existing `-npoints`, `-polydegree`, and `-rbfsmooth` aliases for backward compatibility. Update the top docstring `Script defaults` rows and `Menu UI` rows to use the standards-preferred long option identifiers. Add `--verbose|-v` to argparse, the docstring table, and the General menu section.\n- Planned change: Use `args.verbose` only for extra diagnostics, such as optional traceback or additional path/processor details in per-file exception handling. Keep default output concise.\n- Preserve: Existing Siril-only execution flow, default values `100`, `2`, and `0.1`, output path behavior, `--in-place` and `--overwrite` semantics, existing single-dash aliases, and connect-once/process-all/disconnect behavior.\n- Verification: Run `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/siril_pycache /home/scott/.local/share/siril/venv/bin/python -m py_compile scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py`. Run an AST/docstring inspection to confirm argparse exposes `--npoints`, `--polydegree`, `--rbfsmooth`, and `--verbose|-v`, and that each appears in `Script defaults`.\n\n### Task 2: Update GraXpert docstring aliases and add verbose support\n\n- Files: `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py`\n- Issues addressed: `batch_graxpert.py` undocumented argparse aliases; `batch_graxpert.py` missing `--verbose|-v`.\n- Planned change: Update each affected `Script defaults` row to include all public argparse aliases from the audit, using the long flag first. Examples: `--background|-bg|-bge`, `--denoise|-dn|-denoise`, `--correction|-correction`, `--psfsize|-psfsize|-psf-size`, `--gpu|-gpu`, and `--listmodels|-listmodels`.\n- Planned change: Add `--verbose|-v` to argparse, the `Script defaults` table, and the Advanced or General menu section. Use `args.verbose` for extra diagnostics or tracebacks on per-file/stage failures while preserving concise default logging.\n- Preserve: Existing legacy aliases, model selection behavior, GPU/`--nogpu` behavior, `--operation` menu mode, custom multi-stage ordering, output and intermediate-directory behavior, `--listmodels` running without `input_path`, and connect-once/process-all/disconnect behavior.\n- Verification: Run `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/siril_pycache /home/scott/.local/share/siril/venv/bin/python -m py_compile scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py`. Run an AST/docstring inspection to confirm all argparse aliases are represented in `Script defaults`, including `--verbose|-v`.\n\n### Task 3: Preserve duplicate Script defaults behavior rows in the menu parser\n\n- Files: `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py`\n- Issues addressed: `.batch_ops_menu.py` overwrites repeated `(behavior)` rows in `parse_script_defaults_docstring()`.\n- Planned change: Preserve all parsed `Script defaults` rows in order while keeping the existing lookup behavior for real CLI arguments. Preferred approach: add an ordered list field such as `default_rows: list[DefaultSpec]` to `ScriptInfo`, have the parser collect rows into that list, and keep `defaults` as the current dictionary for argument lookup. Avoid changing call sites that rely on `script.defaults.get(...)` unless necessary.\n- Planned change: If adding a new field is too invasive, use unique internal keys for duplicate behavior rows, such as `(behavior)#1`, `(behavior)#2`, while preserving existing argument lookup keys. The ordered-list approach is preferred because it avoids synthetic keys leaking into display logic.\n- Preserve: Current tooltip lookup, fallback default precedence, argument parsing from `argparse`, `Menu UI` parsing, command-line construction, hidden-file discovery, and log colorization.\n- Verification: Run `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/siril_pycache /home/scott/.local/share/siril/venv/bin/python -m py_compile scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py`. Run a parser check against `FITs_resize.py` and `batch_graxpert.py` proving all `(behavior)` rows are retained in the new ordered storage and existing `defaults` lookups still work for CLI arguments.\n\n### Task 4: Run focused regression checks\n\n- Files: No source files expected; this task verifies changes from Tasks 1-3.\n- Issues addressed: All listed audit issues.\n- Planned change: No code edits. Run syntax and parser checks after implementation.\n- Preserve: No generated `__pycache__` under `scripts/batch_ops`; use `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/siril_pycache`.\n- Verification: Run `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/siril_pycache /home/scott/.local/share/siril/venv/bin/python -m py_compile scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py`. Run an AST-based audit helper that compares argparse arguments against the `Script defaults` table for the modified scripts. Run a menu-parser helper that confirms `parse_script_args()` discovers the modified options and that duplicate behavior rows are retained.\n\n## Required Changelog Task\n\n- Write changelog to:\n  `/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/audit/changelogs/20260625191819_change.md`\n- Document every file changed.\n- Map each change back to the audit issue or planned task.\n- Include verification results.\n- Include deferred issues, if any.\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n- `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/tmp/siril_pycache /home/scott/.local/share/siril/venv/bin/python -m py_compile scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py`\n- AST/docstring check for `batch_auto_bge.py`: confirm `--npoints`, `--polydegree`, `--rbfsmooth`, and `--verbose|-v` are present in argparse and documented in `Script defaults`.\n- AST/docstring check for `batch_graxpert.py`: confirm every argparse alias listed in the source audit is represented in the `Script defaults` table, and that `--verbose|-v` is present in argparse and the table.\n- Menu parser check for `.batch_ops_menu.py`: confirm all `(behavior)` rows from `FITs_resize.py` and `batch_graxpert.py` are retained, and that existing `script.defaults` lookup still returns metadata for normal CLI args such as `--scale`, `--operation`, `--bg-model`, and `output_path`.\n- Optional smoke check: run each modified script with `--help` under the Siril Python environment if imports are available without a live Siril session; if imports fail because Siril/GraXpert modules require runtime context, record that limitation in the changelog.\n\n## Deferred Or Out-Of-Scope\n\n- Re-auditing or changing scripts listed as having no issues: `FITS2IMG.py`, `FITs_resize.py`, and `IGM_resize.py`.\n- Converting single-input scripts to the newer multiple-input CLI shape; the audit did not request that change.\n- Removing legacy single-dash GraXpert or AutoBGE aliases; preserve them for compatibility unless a future audit or user request explicitly asks to remove them.\nEOF","files":[".batch_ops_menu.py",".script_standards.md","/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py","/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/.script_standards.md","/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/audit/changelogs/20260625191819_change.md","/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/audit/results/20260625191819.md","/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py","/home/scott/Documents/siril/scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py","FITS2IMG.py","FITs_resize.py","IGM_resize.py","batch_auto_bge.py","batch_graxpert.py","scripts/batch_ops/.batch_ops_menu.py","scripts/batch_ops/audit/plans/20260625191819_plan.md","scripts/batch_ops/batch_auto_bge.py","scripts/batch_ops/batch_graxpert.py"],"category":"read"}
